1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,999
Chapter 35. The mast head.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,999
It was during the more pleasant weather that in due rotation with the other

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,519
seamen, my first mast head came round.

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:17,758
In most American whalemen, the mast heads are manned almost simultaneously

5
00:00:17,759 --> 00:00:22,877
with the vessels leaving her port, even though she may have 15,000 mi and more

6
00:00:22,878 --> 00:00:27,839
to sail, air reaching her proper cruising ground. And if after a three,

7
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:32,557
four, or five years voyage she is drawing nigh home with anything empty in

8
00:00:32,558 --> 00:00:38,399
her, say an empty vial even, then her mast heads are kept mound to the last,

9
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,199
and not till her sky sail poles sail in amongst the spires of the port does she

10
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,839
altogether relinquish the hope of capturing one whale more.

11
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:53,359
Now, as this business of standing mast heads, a shore or a float, is a very

12
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:58,796
ancient and interesting one, let us in some measure expatiate here. I take it

13
00:00:58,797 --> 00:01:03,278
that the earliest standards of mast heads were the old Egyptians, because in

14
00:01:03,279 --> 00:01:08,717
all my researches I find none prior to them. For though their progenitors, the

15
00:01:08,718 --> 00:01:13,359
builders of Babel, must doubtless by their tower have intended to rear the

16
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:19,839
loftiest mast head in all Asia or Africa either, yet the final truck was put to

17
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:25,039
it, as that great stone mast of theirs may be said to have gone by the board in

18
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:27,519
the dread gale of God's wrath.

19
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:31,199
Therefore, we cannot give these Babelbuilders priority over the

20
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:36,079
Egyptians. And that the Egyptians were a nation of mast head standards is an

21
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:40,478
assertion based upon the general belief among archaeologists that the first

22
00:01:40,479 --> 00:01:45,839
pyramids were founded for astronomical purposes. A theory singularly supported

23
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:51,118
by the peculiar stair-like formation of all four sides of those edififices

24
00:01:51,119 --> 00:01:56,158
whereby with predigious long upliftings of their legs, those old astronomers

25
00:01:56,159 --> 00:02:01,519
were want to mount to the apex and sing out for new stars even as the lookouts

26
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:07,199
of a modern ship sing out for a sail or a whale just bearing in sight. In St.

27
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:12,476
Stylites, the famous Christian hermit of old times, who built him a lofty stone

28
00:02:12,477 --> 00:02:16,318
pillar in the desert, and spent the whole latter portion of his life on its

29
00:02:16,319 --> 00:02:21,438
summit, hoisting his food from the ground with a tackle. In him we have a

30
00:02:21,439 --> 00:02:26,239
remarkable instance of a dauntless stander of mast heads, who was not to be

31
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:32,239
driven from his place by fogs or frosts, rain, hail, or sleet, but valiantly

32
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:37,598
facing everything out to the last, literally died at his post. Of modern

33
00:02:37,599 --> 00:02:42,636
standards of mast heads, we have but a lifeless set, mere stone, iron, and

34
00:02:42,637 --> 00:02:47,839
bronze men, who, though well capable of facing out a stiff gale, are entirely

35
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:52,717
incompetent to the business of singing out upon discovering any strange sight.

36
00:02:52,718 --> 00:02:58,158
There is Napoleon who upon the top of the column of Van Don stands with arms

37
00:02:58,159 --> 00:03:04,877
folded some 150 ft in the air, careless now who rules the decks below, whether

38
00:03:04,878 --> 00:03:10,636
Louis Phipe, Louis Blanc or Louis the Devil, Great Washington, too stands high

39
00:03:10,637 --> 00:03:15,598
aloft on his towering main mast in Baltimore, and like one of Hercules

40
00:03:15,599 --> 00:03:20,557
pillars, his column marks that point of human grandeur beyond which few mortals

41
00:03:20,558 --> 00:03:26,318
will go. Admiral Nelson also on a capston of gunmetal stands his mast head

42
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:32,158
in Trfalgar Square. And ever when most obscured by that London smoke token is

43
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:35,359
yet given that a hidden hero is there.

44
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:40,239
For where there is smoke there must be fire. But neither great Washington nor

45
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:46,079
Napoleon nor Nelson will answer a single hail from below. However madly invoked

46
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:50,956
to befriend by their councils the distracted decks upon which they gaze.

47
00:03:50,957 --> 00:03:55,199
However, it may be surmised that their spirits penetrate through the thick haze

48
00:03:55,200 --> 00:04:00,636
of the future, and describe what schos and what rocks must be shunned.

49
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:05,199
It may seem unwarrantable to couple in any respect the mast head standards of

50
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:10,079
the land with those of the sea, but that in truth it is not so, is plainly

51
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:15,679
evinced by an item for which Obed Macy, the sole historian of Nantucket, stands

52
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:20,318
accountable. The worthy oed tells us that in the early times of the whale

53
00:04:20,319 --> 00:04:24,877
fishery, air ships were regularly launched in pursuit of the game, the

54
00:04:24,878 --> 00:04:29,758
people of that island erected lofty spars along the sea coast to which the

55
00:04:29,759 --> 00:04:34,476
lookouts ascended by means of nailed cleats, something as fowls go upstairs

56
00:04:34,477 --> 00:04:39,438
in a hen house. A few years ago, this same plan was adopted by the Bay

57
00:04:39,439 --> 00:04:44,079
Whaleman of New Zealand, who upon describing the game gave notice to the

58
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:49,839
readyman boats neither beach. But this custom has now become obsolete. Turn we

59
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:55,118
then to the one proper mast head, that of a whale ship at sea. The three mast

60
00:04:55,119 --> 00:05:00,079
heads are kept man from sunrise to sunset, the seammen taking their regular

61
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:05,839
turns as at the helm, and relieving each other every 2 hours. In the serene

62
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:10,158
weather of the tropics, it is exceedingly pleasant, the mast head.

63
00:05:10,159 --> 00:05:16,318
Nay, to a dreamy, meditative man, it is delightful. There you stand 100 ft above

64
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:21,039
the silent decks, striding along the deep, as if the mass were gigantic

65
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:25,839
stilts, while beneath you, and between your legs, as it were, swim the hugest

66
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:30,877
monsters of the sea. Even as ships once sailed between the boots of the famous

67
00:05:30,878 --> 00:05:37,039
Colossus at old roads, there you stand, lost in the infinite series of the sea.

68
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:42,079
With nothing ruffled but the waves, the transed ship indolently rolls. The

69
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:47,598
drowsy trade winds blow. Everything resolves you into a langor. For the most

70
00:05:47,599 --> 00:05:52,956
part in this tropic whailing life, the sublime uneventfulness invests you. You

71
00:05:52,957 --> 00:05:58,158
hear no news, read no gazettes. Extras with startling accounts of common places

72
00:05:58,159 --> 00:06:03,118
never delude you into unnecessary excitements. You hear of no domestic

73
00:06:03,119 --> 00:06:08,079
afflictions, bankrupt securities, fall of stocks, are never troubled with the

74
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:12,239
thought of what you shall have for dinner, for all your meals for 3 years

75
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:18,079
and more are snugly stowed in casks, and your bill of fair is immutable.

76
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:22,796
In one of those southern whalemen on a long three or four years voyage, as

77
00:06:22,797 --> 00:06:27,519
often happens, the sum of the various hours you spend at the mast head would

78
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:32,717
amount to several entire months. And it is much to be deplored that the place to

79
00:06:32,718 --> 00:06:36,158
which you devote so considerable a portion of the whole term of your

80
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:40,717
natural life should be so sadly destitute of anything approaching to a

81
00:06:40,718 --> 00:06:46,877
cozy inhabitiveness or adapted to breed a comfortable localess of feeling such

82
00:06:46,878 --> 00:06:52,476
as pertains to a bed, a hammock, a hearse, a sentry box, a pullpit, a

83
00:06:52,477 --> 00:06:57,039
coach, or any other of those small and snug contrivances in which men

84
00:06:57,040 --> 00:07:02,239
temporarily isolate themselves. Your most usual point of perch is the head of

85
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:07,278
the tag gallant mast where you stand upon two thin parallel sticks almost

86
00:07:07,279 --> 00:07:12,239
peculiar to whaleman called the tag gallant cross trees. Here tossed about

87
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:16,956
by the sea the beginner feels about as cozy as he would standing on a bull's

88
00:07:16,957 --> 00:07:22,239
horns. To be sure, in cold weather you may carry your house a loft with you in

89
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:26,717
the shape of a watchcoat, but properly speaking, the thickest watch coat is no

90
00:07:26,718 --> 00:07:29,598
more of a house than the unclad body.

91
00:07:29,599 --> 00:07:34,476
For as the soul is glued inside of its fleshy tabernacle, and cannot freely

92
00:07:34,477 --> 00:07:38,636
move about in it, nor even move out of it without running great risk of

93
00:07:38,637 --> 00:07:43,839
perishing, like an ignorant pilgrim crossing the snowy Alps in winter. So a

94
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:49,039
watch code is not so much of a house as it is a mere envelope or additional skin

95
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:54,476
encasing you. You cannot put a shelf or chest of drawers in your body, and no

96
00:07:54,477 --> 00:07:58,717
more can you make a convenient closet of your watch coat.

97
00:07:58,718 --> 00:08:02,399
Concerning all this, it is much to be deplored that the mast heads of a

98
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:06,877
southern whale ship are unprovided with those enviable little tents or pullpits

99
00:08:06,878 --> 00:08:10,956
called crow's nests, in which the lookouts of a Greenland whaler are

100
00:08:10,957 --> 00:08:15,359
protected from the inclement weather of the frozen seas. In the fireside

101
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:20,239
narrative of Captain Sleet, entitled A Voyage Among the Icebergs in Quest of

102
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:24,956
the Greenland Whale and incidentally for the rediscovery of the Lost Icelandic

103
00:08:24,957 --> 00:08:30,079
Colonies of Old Greenland. In this admirable volume, all standards of mast

104
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:34,318
heads are furnished with a charmingly circumstantial account of the then

105
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:39,039
recently invented Crow's Nest of the Glacier, which was the name of Captain

106
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:44,318
Sleet's Good Craft. He called it the Sleet's crow's nest in honor of himself.

107
00:08:44,319 --> 00:08:48,956
He being the original inventor and patentee and free from all ridiculous

108
00:08:48,957 --> 00:08:53,199
false delicacy and holding that if we call our own children after our own

109
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:58,956
names, we fathers being the original inventors and patentees. So likewise we

110
00:08:58,957 --> 00:09:04,158
should denominate after ourselves any other apparatus we may beget. In shape

111
00:09:04,159 --> 00:09:09,519
the sleet crow's nest is something like a large tears pipe. It is open above,

112
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:13,918
however, where it is furnished with a movable side screen to keep to windward

113
00:09:13,919 --> 00:09:18,796
of your head in a hard gale. Being fixed on the summit of the mast, you ascend

114
00:09:18,797 --> 00:09:23,519
into it through a little trap hatch in the bottom. On the after side, or the

115
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:27,278
side next to the stern of the ship, is a comfortable seat with a locker

116
00:09:27,279 --> 00:09:32,476
underneath for umbrellas, comforters, and coats. In front is a leather rack in

117
00:09:32,477 --> 00:09:36,399
which to keep your speaking trumpet, pipe, telescope, and other nautical

118
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:40,796
conveniences. When Captain Sleet in person stood his mast head in this

119
00:09:40,797 --> 00:09:45,679
crow's nest of his, he tells us that he always had a rifle with him, also fixed

120
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:49,999
in the rack, together with a powder flask and shot for the purpose of

121
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,359
popping off the stray naral or vagrant sea unicorns infesting those waters, for

122
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:59,039
you cannot successfully shoot at them from the deck owing to the resistance of

123
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:04,158
the water. But to shoot down upon them is a very different thing. Now, it was

124
00:10:04,159 --> 00:10:08,557
plainly a labor of love for Captain Sleet to describe as he does all the

125
00:10:08,558 --> 00:10:13,598
little detailed conveniences of his crow's nest, but though he so enlarges

126
00:10:13,599 --> 00:10:18,476
upon many of these, and though he treats us to a very scientific account of his

127
00:10:18,477 --> 00:10:22,717
experiments in this crow's nest, with a small compass he kept there for the

128
00:10:22,718 --> 00:10:27,519
purpose of counteracting the errors resulting from what is called the local

129
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:32,318
attraction of all binnacle magnets, an error ascribable to the horizontal

130
00:10:32,319 --> 00:10:36,399
vicinity of the iron in the ship's planks, and in the glacier's case

131
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:41,039
perhaps to there having been so many broken down blacksmiths among her crew.

132
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:45,039
I say that though the captain is very discreet and scientific here, yet for

133
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:49,999
all his learned binnacle deviations, azimuth compass observations, and

134
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:55,359
approximate errors, he knows very well, Captain Sleet, that he was not so much

135
00:10:55,360 --> 00:11:00,557
immersed in those profound magnetic meditations as to fail being attracted

136
00:11:00,558 --> 00:11:04,318
occasionally towards that well-relenished little case bottle so

137
00:11:04,319 --> 00:11:08,956
nicely tucked in on one side of his crow's nest within easy reach of his

138
00:11:08,957 --> 00:11:13,999
hand. Though upon the whole I greatly admire and even love the brave, the

139
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,476
honest and learned captain, yet I take it very ill of him that he should so

140
00:11:18,477 --> 00:11:23,199
utterly ignore that case bottle, seeing what a faithful friend and comforter it

141
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:27,679
must have been, while with mittened fingers and hooded head, he was studying

142
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:34,158
the mathematics a loft there in that bird's nest within three or four perches of the pole.

143
00:11:34,159 --> 00:11:39,039
But if we southern whale fishers are not so snugly housed aloft as Captain Sleet

144
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:43,679
and his Greenland men were, yet that disadvantage is greatly counterbalanced

145
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:48,717
by the widely contrasting serenity of those seductive seas in which we

146
00:11:48,718 --> 00:11:53,758
southers mostly float. For one, I used to lounge up in the rigging very

147
00:11:53,759 --> 00:11:59,278
leisurely, resting in the top to have a chat with Quiqu or anyone else off duty

148
00:11:59,279 --> 00:12:03,999
whom I might find there. Then ascending a little way further and throwing a lazy

149
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,956
leg over the topppsil yard, take a preliminary view of the watery pastures,

150
00:12:08,957 --> 00:12:13,519
and so at last mount to my ultimate destination.

151
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:18,318
Let me make a clean breast of it here, and frankly admit that I kept but sorry

152
00:12:18,319 --> 00:12:24,399
guard. With the problem of the universe revolving in me, how could I, being left

153
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:29,278
completely to myself, at such a thought engendering altitude, how could I but

154
00:12:29,279 --> 00:12:34,158
lightly hold my obligations to observe all whale ships standing orders, keep

155
00:12:34,159 --> 00:12:39,199
your weather eye open, and sing out every time? And let me in this place

156
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:44,158
movingly admonish you, you ship owners of Nantucket, beware of enlisting in

157
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:49,118
your vigilant fisheries any lad with lean brow and hollow eye given to

158
00:12:49,119 --> 00:12:54,079
unseasonable meditiveness, and who offers to ship with the Fedan instead of

159
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:59,519
Bowitch in his head. Beware of such a one, I say. Your whales must be seen

160
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:03,918
before they can be killed. And this sunkeneyed young platonist will tow you

161
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:09,438
10 wakes round the world and never make you one pint of sperm the richer. Nor

162
00:13:09,439 --> 00:13:14,956
are these munitions at all unneeded. For nowadays the whale fishery furnishes an

163
00:13:14,957 --> 00:13:20,717
asylum for many romantic, melancholy, and absent-minded young men disgusted

164
00:13:20,718 --> 00:13:25,999
with the carking cares of earth and seeking sentiment in tar and blubber.

165
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:30,079
Child Harold not infrequently perches himself upon the mast head of some

166
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:35,598
luckless disappointed whale ship and in moody phrase ejaculates.

167
00:13:35,599 --> 00:13:39,278
Roll on thou deep dark blue ocean roll.

168
00:13:39,279 --> 00:13:43,999
10,000 blubber hunters sweep over thee in vain.

169
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:48,399
Very often do the captains of such ships take those absent-minded young

170
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:53,598
philosophers to task, upgrading them with not feeling sufficient interest in

171
00:13:53,599 --> 00:13:58,158
the voyage, half hinting that they are so hopelessly lost to all honorable

172
00:13:58,159 --> 00:14:02,956
ambition, as that in their secret souls they would rather not see whales than

173
00:14:02,957 --> 00:14:08,158
otherwise, but all in vain. Those young platonists have a notion that their

174
00:14:08,159 --> 00:14:12,877
vision is imperfect. They are shortsighted. What use then to strain

175
00:14:12,878 --> 00:14:19,199
the visual nerve? They have left their opera glasses at home. Why thou monkey?

176
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,598
said a harpooner to one of these lads.

177
00:14:21,599 --> 00:14:26,476
We've been cruising now hard upon 3 years, and thou hast not raised a whale

178
00:14:26,477 --> 00:14:31,918
yet. Whales are scarce as hen's teeth whenever thou art up here. Perhaps they

179
00:14:31,919 --> 00:14:36,956
were, or perhaps there might have been Schos of them in the far horizon, but

180
00:14:36,957 --> 00:14:41,519
lulled into such an opium-like listlessness of vacant unconscious

181
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:46,557
revery is this absent-minded youth by the blending cadence of waves with

182
00:14:46,558 --> 00:14:51,839
thoughts that at last he loses his identity, takes the mystic ocean at his

183
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:57,598
feet for the visible image of that deep blue bottomless soul pervading mankind

184
00:14:57,599 --> 00:15:04,079
and nature, and every strange half-seen gliding beautiful thing that eludes him.

185
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:10,717
Every dimly discovered uprising fin of some undicernable form seems to him the

186
00:15:10,718 --> 00:15:15,918
embodiment of those elusive thoughts that only people the soul by continually

187
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:21,438
flitting through it. In this enchanted mood, thy spirit ebs away to whence it

188
00:15:21,439 --> 00:15:25,999
came, becomes diffused through time and space like Kramer's sprinkled

189
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:33,519
pantheistic ashes, forming at last a part of every shore the round globe over.

190
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:38,717
There is no life in thee now except that rocking life imparted by a gently

191
00:15:38,718 --> 00:15:44,557
rolling ship by her borrowed from the sea, by the sea from the inscrable tides

192
00:15:44,558 --> 00:15:50,476
of God. But while this sleep, this dream is on you, move your foot or hand an

193
00:15:50,477 --> 00:15:56,956
inch, slip your hold at all, and your identity comes back in horror. Over

194
00:15:56,957 --> 00:16:02,318
decartian vortices you hover, and perhaps at midday, in the fairest

195
00:16:02,319 --> 00:16:07,519
weather, with one halfthrottled shriek, you drop through that transparent air

196
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:16,200
into the summer sea, no more to rise forever. Heed it well, you pantheists.
